every forward case lowers a contraction nest with output and reduction loops, raw and optimized: true
forward lowering opens every output loop before any reduction loop, raw and optimized: true
the predicate refuses the matmul with its reduction loop interchanged above an output loop: true
backprop lowers a weight gradient's batch reduction loop OUTSIDE its output loops (the order is a forward-lowering property only): true
the bf16 legs find a contraction nest of each gradient, raw and optimized: true
a bf16 dense layer's weight and input gradients both lower reduction-outer raw: true
the optimized routine opens every output loop of both bf16 gradients before its reductions: true
an f32 weight gradient keeps its batch reduction outermost in the optimized routine: true
the bf16 window input gradient lowers over the forward window and channel loops: true
the optimized bf16 window input gradient opens its cell loop before all reductions: true
the bf16 two-dimensional window input gradient lowers over the forward window and channel loops: true
the optimized bf16 two-dimensional window input gradient opens both cell loops before all reductions: true
an f32 two-dimensional window input gradient preserves its lowered reduction-outer loop order in the optimized routine: true
